      "question": {
        "math_academy_id": "q-130848",
        "knowledge_point_id": "9a0ab53e-79ff-5520-bb50-069fd381d29d",
        "knowledge_point": "Identifying a Row Operation Given the Connection Between Two Determinants",
        "problem": "Given that $det(A)=det(B),$ which of the following elementary row operations transforms matrix $A$ to matrix $B,$ where\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -8 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]?\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "Since $det(A)=det(B)$, the row operation applied to $A$ must be to add or subtract a multiple of one row to another row. In other words, it is of the form \n\n$$\n{R}_{j}:={R}_{j}+(k){R}_{i},\\,i\\ne j.\n$$\n\nBy considering the given row operations that are of the above form, we notice that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(A) & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 1 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}| & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{3} \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & -8 & 10 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 1 & 2 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =det(B).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the required row operation is\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+(-3){R}_{3}.\n$$",
        "answer_fields": [
          {
