        "problem": "Find $x$, if $2a+5x=b$ and\n\n$$\na=[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -30 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
        "worked_solution": "Using the properties of addition/subtraction and scalar multiplication of vectors to isolate $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2a+5x & =b \\\\ 5x & =b-2a \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{5}(b-2a) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{5}([\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -30 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}]-2[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -5 \\\\ -10\\end{aligned}]) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{5}[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ -20 \\\\ 40\\end{aligned}] \\\\ x & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 8\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
