        "knowledge_point": "Solving for Three Coefficients in a Linear Combination",
        "problem": "Consider the vectors\n\n$$\n{a}_{1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{2}=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}],\\,{a}_{3}=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nIf ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b,$ then what is ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}?$",
        "worked_solution": "If ${x}_{1}{a}_{1}+{x}_{2}{a}_{2}+{x}_{3}{a}_{3}=b$, then we have  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ -8 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 5 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ 3{x}_{1} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{2} \\\\ -8{x}_{2} \\\\ 6{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}2{x}_{3} \\\\ 5{x}_{3} \\\\ -3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3} \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3} \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, we get the following system:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-8{x}_{2}+5{x}_{3}=1 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+6{x}_{2}-3{x}_{3}=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe will solve this system using Gaussian elimination. First, we write the augmented matrix for this system:\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 6 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nRow-reducing the augmented matrix, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 3 & -8 & 5 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 6 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -5 \\\\ -2 & 6 & -3 & 2\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -1 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 6\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe system is now \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+2{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ {x}_{2}-{x}_{3}=-5 \\\\ {x}_{3}=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the third equation, we get ${x}_{3}=6.$ Substituting ${x}_{3}=6$ into the second equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{2}-6=-5\\,⟹\\,{x}_{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting ${x}_{2}=1$ and ${x}_{3}=6$ into the first equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3(1)+2(6)=2\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=-7.\n$$\n\nSo, the solution of the system is ${x}_{1}=-7$, ${x}_{2}=1$, and ${x}_{3}=6,$ which means \n\n$$\n-7{a}_{1}+{a}_{2}+6{a}_{3}=b.\n$$\n\nConsequently, \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}=-7+1+6=0.\n$$",
